// Package wayland implements platform.Platform on Wayland without cgo.
// libwayland-client and libxkbcommon are opened with purego, and every function
// is resolved at startup.
//
// The bindings of the protocols in protocol/ are generated by cmd/gowaku-bindgen.
// Requests go through wl_proxy_marshal_array_flags, and all events through one
// dispatcher, so that the number of purego callbacks does not grow with the
// protocols. The title bar comes from the compositor when it offers
// xdg-decoration, and is otherwise drawn by the application (ClientDecorated).
// See docs/ADR/0021-wayland-platform.md.
//
// Bindings of other protocols, which cmd/gowaku-bindgen writes in a package of
// the program, run on the same connection: Platform.Globals and Platform.Bind
// reach the registry, and Conn, Interface, Proxy, Args and Listen are what the
// generated code calls. See docs/ADR/0077-wayland-bindgen.md.
//
// This is one of the few packages allowed to use unsafe and purego.
package wayland

//go:generate go run ../../cmd/gowaku-bindgen -runtime= -out vpointer_gpu_linux_test.go -table testInterfaces -tags "linux && gpu" testdata/wlr-virtual-pointer-unstable-v1.xml
//go:generate go run ../../cmd/gowaku-bindgen -runtime= -out protocol_linux.go -skip wl_shell,wl_shell_surface protocol/wayland.xml protocol/xdg-shell.xml protocol/xdg-decoration-unstable-v1.xml protocol/fractional-scale-v1.xml protocol/viewporter.xml protocol/cursor-shape-v1.xml protocol/text-input-unstable-v3.xml protocol/xdg-foreign-unstable-v2.xml protocol/pointer-gestures-unstable-v1.xml protocol/tablet-unstable-v2.xml protocol/xdg-toplevel-icon-v1.xml
